From e.pebesma at geo.uu.nl  Mon Jan 22 15:11:25 2007
From: e.pebesma at geo.uu.nl (Edzer J. Pebesma)
Date: Mon Jan 22 15:11:25 2007
Subject: [STATSGRASS] gstat: problem with prediction value at point
	location
In-Reply-To: <45B5153C.7010200@amu.edu.pl>
References: <45B5153C.7010200@amu.edu.pl>
Message-ID: <45B51A6D.5090503@geo.uu.nl>

This is a well-known property of kriging if locations coincide exactly: 
if measured, the best estimate is the measurement itself. It's also 
cause of the problem that you can't have duplicate observations in 
kriging. Even with a nugget, gamma(0)=0. You may want to shift your 
points or your grid e.g. a few centimeters to get rid of it.
--
Edzer

